<in-bse-fin:DisclosureOfNotesOnFinancialResultsExplanatoryTextBlock contextRef="OneD">1.The above Consolidated Unaudited Financial Results for the Quarter &amp; year ended 31.03.2020 have been reviewed and recommended by the Audit Committee and approved  by the Board of Directors at their meeting held on 25.07.2020. The results for the year ended March 31, 2020 has been audited and for the quarter ended March 31, 2020 has been reviewed by our statutory auditors. The statutory auditors of the Company have expressed an unmodified opinion thereon.  n2.Consolidated Financial Statements have been prepared in accordance with Accounting Standard-21 issued by ICAI. Consolidated Results are combined numbers of  Vivimed Labs Limited and its  direct wholly owned subsidiaries, viz., (i) Finoso Pharma Pvt Limited (ii) Vivimed Speciality chemicals Pvt ltd  and its wholly owned foreign subsidaries viz(i) Vivimed Labs USA, Inc.,(ii)Vivimed Labs Mauritius Limited (iii) Vivimed Holdings Limited and its Step-down subsidiaries  (iv) Vivimed Labs Europe Limited ( divested in Q2) (v) Vivimed Labs UK Limited, (vi) Vivimed Labs Spain, S.L. (vii) Union Quimico Farmaceutica S.A.U., Spain, (viii) Holliday International Limited,UK &amp; (ix) Uquifa Mexico S.A. de C.V.(x) UQUIFA Sciences (MASCARENE) Ltd (xi) Soneas Chemicals Ltd (xii) Soneas Research Ltd and its wholly owned Indian subsidiary  (i) UQUIFA India Private Limited.  n3. In line with provisions of Ind AS 108 Operating segments, the Company has primarily two segments  speciality chemicals  and  Pharma  and accordingly considered under reportable segments by the Company.  n4.During the year ended March 31, 2020, the Company allotted 3,90,000 equity shares of Rs.2/ - each, consequent to the exercise of the stock options by the employees of the Company under the Employee Stock Option Plan.  n  n5.COVID-19 is the infectious disease caused by the most recently discovered coronavirus, SARS-CoV-2. In March 2020, the WHO declared COVID-19 a pandemic. The Group has adopted measures to curb the spread of infection in order to protect the health of our employees and ensure business continuity with minimal disruption.In assessing the recoverability of receivables and other financials assets, the Group has considered internal and external information upto the date of approval of these consolidated financial results. The impact of the global health pandemic may be different from that of estimated as at the date of approval of these consolidated financial results and the Group will continue to closely monitor any material changes to future economic conditions.  n6.Corresponding numbers of previous period / year have been regrouped, wherever necessary.</in-bse-fin:DisclosureOfNotesOnFinancialResultsExplanatoryTextBlock>
